            <p>To record a podcast in Bangkok with professional sound quality, you need a room with proper acoustic treatment and quality microphones. Thunder Studio's <a href={`/${lang}/rooms/control-room`}>Control Room</a> in Bang Khen offers a mixing console, DAW workstation, and studio monitors — covering solo hosts, two-person interviews, and full panel recordings.</p>

            <h2>What is a podcast studio?</h2>
            <p>A podcast studio is a recording space designed specifically for vocal recording. The key factor isn't just the equipment — it's the room's acoustics. An untreated room produces echo that sounds unprofessional, regardless of how expensive your microphone is.</p>
            <p>At Thunder Studio, the <a href={`/${lang}/rooms/control-room`}>Control Room</a> handles both music recording and podcast recording. It's designed for clean acoustics, low external noise bleed, and a monitoring system that lets you hear every detail of spoken audio during recording.</p>

            <h2>Equipment needed for podcast recording</h2>
            <p>A quality podcast recording requires these key items:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Condenser or dynamic microphone</strong> — Condenser mics like AKG or Neumann capture voice detail beautifully but require a treated room. Dynamic mics like the Shure SM7B reject background noise better, making them more forgiving in imperfect rooms.</li>
              <li><strong>Audio interface or mixing console</strong> — Converts the mic signal to digital and controls gain so audio doesn't clip or sit too quietly.</li>
              <li><strong>DAW workstation</strong> — Recording software like Pro Tools or Logic Pro, used to capture, edit, remove noise, and export the final file.</li>
              <li><strong>Monitoring headphones</strong> — For listening to playback and checking audio quality during the session.</li>
              <li><strong>Acoustic treatment</strong> — Foam panels or absorbers that reduce room reflections. Without them, even great microphones capture a roomy, unprofessional sound.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Thunder Studio's Control Room has all of the above ready to use. No need to bring your own gear. See full details on the <a href={`/${lang}/services`}>services page</a>.</p>

