            <p><strong>What microphone do I need for a podcast?</strong><br />Dynamic microphones like the Shure SM7B are forgiving in rooms with imperfect acoustics and reject background noise well. Condenser microphones capture more detail but require a properly treated room. A professional studio has both types and can advise which suits your voice and content.</p>

            <p><strong>Can I record a podcast interview with a guest in the same studio?</strong><br />Yes. In-person podcast interviews require multiple microphones and a mixing console with enough input channels. Thunder Studio's Control Room supports multi-mic setups for solo hosts, two-person interviews, and panel discussions.</p>

